{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UfyPw1rb54PyWvFmzFQxMd","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78fe79ca-00fe-4179-aa95-c5eccecb1b0f","uuid":"88dd0f09-4971-4319-95e8-98d8d746f813","timestamp":"2026-06-11T04:16:34.071Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- **sos_1 \"may cast target\" decision flow:**","newString":"- **sos_97 simplifications:** surveil keeps the non-binned cards in their original\n  order (\"any order\" not modeled); the −1 lets each targeted player choose their\n  own discard; the −2 re-checks creature-type/MV ≤ 3/zone at resolution and\n  fizzles silently otherwise. Skipped turns consume `player.skip_turns` inside\n  `advance_phase`'s wrap-around, so extra turns granted to other players still\n  insert correctly.\n- **sos_1 \"may cast target\" decision flow:**","originalFile":"# Key decisions log\n\n- **E1 also fires in `cast_spell_free`.** TODO named only `cast_spell`, but rule\n  601.2 makes free/alternative casts real casts (magecraft-style triggers fire for\n  them). Copies made by `copy_spell` still bypass it, as intended.\n- **sos_1 needed two engine fixes the plan assumed already worked:** the engine never\n  fired `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (added to `declare_attackers_step`, after all attackers\n  are declared, per rule 508.1) and never consulted replacement effects for a resolving\n  spell's stack→graveyard move (added `SpellGraveyardReplacementEvent`, passed by\n  `_resolve_spell`; `move_to_zone` now consults replacements for stack moves too).\n- **sos_257 restricted mana:** `ManaPool` tracks a per-type \"instant/sorcery only\"\n  count (`add_restricted`), excluded from payment unless `pay(...,\n  for_instant_sorcery=True)`; `cast_spell` passes that flag based on the spell's\n  types. Restricted mana is spent before unrestricted mana of the same type.\n  Deliberate limitations: the only restriction kind modeled is instant/sorcery-only,\n  and activated-ability costs never use restricted mana (correct for this card).\n- **sos_257 animation:** in-place mutation plus a `_reset_characteristics` override\n  (mirroring fdn_244's pattern) so continuous-effect recalculation doesn't wipe the\n  creature type. Animated land is treated as not summoning-sick (it was already on\n  the battlefield). The +1/+0 pump mutates immediately *and* registers an until-EOT\n  effect so both the direct path and an `apply_all` recalculation agree.\n- **sos_57 \"next main phase\" = next precombat main.** The engine has no\n  postcombat-main event; a counter resolved during your own precombat main would\n  in paper grant the mana that turn's postcombat main, here it waits for your next\n  turn. Wizard check happens when the delayed trigger fires (intervening-if\n  re-check), not at Mana Sculpt's resolution. \"Mana spent\" = post-reduction amount\n  actually paid (X = 0), recorded as `card.mana_spent` at cast time.\n- **sos_120 Paradigm copies are cast, not `copy_spell`-ed.** Rule 702.192a: \"create\n  a copy of this object in exile. You may cast the copy without paying its mana\n  cost\" — so a fresh `copy.copy` goes to exile and is cast via `cast_spell_free`\n  (firing cast triggers, correctly). After casting, the copy is flagged `is_token`\n  so the existing token SBA removes it once it leaves the stack — the engine-native\n  way to model \"a copy ceases to exist\". First-resolution tracking is per player and\n  per card name (`controller._paradigm_resolved_names`), per the rule's wording.\n- **sos_13 prepared semantics from rule 722.3:** becoming prepared creates the\n  Swords copy in exile immediately; casting it pays {W} (the rulebook says the copy\n  is *cast*, not cast-for-free — TODO's `cast_spell_free` is still used as the\n  stack path, with {W} paid explicitly first). The \"opponent controls more\n  creatures than you\" comparison counts Emeritus itself (it is entering as the\n  effect resolves, but `on_resolve` runs pre-move, hence a +1). Limitations: if\n  Emeritus leaves the battlefield while prepared the exile copy lingers (but is no\n  longer castable — `cast_prepared_spell` checks battlefield presence); the mana\n  refund on a failed cast is always {W} even if a different type paid the cost.\n- **sos_1 \"may cast target\" decision flow:** one candidate → auto-selected,\n  `choose_yes_no` decides the may; multiple candidates → single `choose_card` where\n  `None` declines. Deliberate limitation: a *countered* free-cast spell is not exiled\n  (the counter path moves cards to the graveyard without consulting replacements).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":41,"oldLines":6,"newStart":41,"newLines":12,"lines":["   Emeritus leaves the battlefield while prepared the exile copy lingers (but is no","   longer castable — `cast_prepared_spell` checks battlefield presence); the mana","   refund on a failed cast is always {W} even if a different type paid the cost.","+- **sos_97 simplifications:** surveil keeps the non-binned cards in their original","+  order (\"any order\" not modeled); the −1 lets each targeted player choose their","+  own discard; the −2 re-checks creature-type/MV ≤ 3/zone at resolution and","+  fizzles silently otherwise. Skipped turns consume `player.skip_turns` inside","+  `advance_phase`'s wrap-around, so extra turns granted to other players still","+  insert correctly."," - **sos_1 \"may cast target\" decision flow:** one candidate → auto-selected,","   `choose_yes_no` decides the may; multiple candidates → single `choose_card` where","   `None` declines. Deliberate limitation: a *countered* free-cast spell is not exiled"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
