{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01GQH44XFQVjzrTwnYHScDUe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. **All ten SOS cards are implemented, tested, and committed** — every TODO.md checklist item is `[x]`, the engine regression suite finishes at 1145 passed (its baseline, no regressions), the full workspace suite is 1258 passed, and all ten card classes construct bare and import cleanly. Eleven commits: one for the shared E1–E3 seams, one per card.\n\n**Shared engine seams built first (E1–E3):** `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` now fires in `cast_spell` *and* `cast_spell_free` (rule 601.2 — free casts are still casts); `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` fires from `GameState.advance_phase` after pools empty; `get_cost_reduction` aggregates `spell_cost_reduction` from the caster's battlefield permanents.\n\n**Places where the plan and the real engine disagreed** (fixed per the engine/spec, logged in `KEY_DECISIONS.md`):\n- `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined but never fired — TODO assumed attack triggers worked. Now fired in `declare_attackers_step` (needed by sos_1).\n- Replacement effects were never consulted for a resolving spell's stack→graveyard move, so TODO's \"exile it instead\" recipe couldn't work. Added `SpellGraveyardReplacementEvent` through the existing replacement manager (sos_1, sos_120's Paradigm self-exile).\n- Self-ETB triggers via `register_triggers` never fire (the engine fires the ETB event before registering the entering card), so sos_13's enter effect follows the fdn_205 convention and lives in `on_resolve`.\n- The rulebook overruled two TODO suggestions: the Paradigm copy is *cast* from exile (so it correctly fires cast triggers) rather than `copy_spell`-ed, and sos_13's prepared Swords copy is cast *paying its {W}*, not free (rule 722.3c).\n\n**Other small additive engine changes, each driven by one card:** restricted instant/sorcery-only mana in `ManaPool` (sos_257), `card.mana_spent` recording (sos_57), seedable `game.rng` plus `skip_turns` consumption in the turn wrap (sos_97), and an optional `targets` parameter on `activate_ability` that mirrors targets into `source.chosen_targets` at resolve time (sos_97). No existing symbols were renamed, moved, or deleted, and `engine_tests/` was never touched.\n\nEach card has 5–9 focused tests driven through `test_utils`, `cast_spell`/`cast_spell_free`, `activate_ability`, and `priority_loop`, plus a throwaway spec-derived smoke check covering a scenario the tests don't (e.g., restricted mana paying a sorcery's generic cost, miracle firing off a loot draw on an opponent's turn, a 5-heads ultimate skipping five consecutive turns)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_read_input_tokens":350774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78fe79ca-00fe-4179-aa95-c5eccecb1b0f","uuid":"1ed65761-372f-4764-9f90-787a193f029c","request_id":"req_011CbvpteGS5S4paaa9uGEo2"}
